Z||000009||Fformula88||03-26-2000||06:12 PM||||Since the day GM pulled the plug on the Fiero, they have tried to hide the fact that they ever made it.  They simply do not mention it at all.  Maybe if enough people express a desire to them to see Fiero parts offered, then they will do it.  However, most of the stuff Fiero owners would like, is either available through a dealer anyway or GM doesn't have ANY of them anymore.  We need someone to begin reproducing interior pieces for restorations (like the center console, radio pod etc).  Everyone email them and complain!||||reg||8
Z||000010||GT Bastard||03-26-2000||08:38 PM||||Earne, I didn't mean to sound defensive but it seems like we keep coming back to this fact.  I'm sure that if GM had alloted more money for the Fiero project, the car would have been more popular and would never have been discontinued. <BR> You said: "I don't believe it is entirely correct to say that we wouldn't have a Fiero if not for GM."<BR>  The chances of another car company putting the Fiero into production would be extremely far-fetched. And even if they did, it wouldn't be the same Fiero we know today. No flames intended to anyone.  ||||reg||1
