Z||000012||GT Bastard||03-26-2000||09:44 PM||||Earne, do you seriously make toys?  What kinds of toys?  I always wanted to be a toy-tester like on the movie 'Big' with Tom Hanks. See ya...||||reg||1
Z||000013||Earne||03-26-2000||10:13 PM||||GT B,<P>I "make" toys for me.  For about 35 years now I have I have been building or restoring various cars.  Dune buggies, BMW Isetta, Triumph TR6, Fiat 850, '65 Bug Panel Van (complete custom, they never existed), 16 other Bugs, '56 Porche, '86 SE (gave to son), '86.5GT, and many I've left out.  I'm just finishing GL1200 Goldwing with the back half and seat of a GL1500 (got to be a Winger to appreciate that),  I usually keep them a few years and pass them along to someone that appreciates the time and effort.<P>I know what you mean by the tester in "Big".  That would be a great job.  In the wings, waiting for more time, is an Indy Fiero go cart body.  I'll start on that next winter.  I'll probably keep it for my grandkids.  Used ToyMaker for a while, changed to Concentric and somebody had the name, just used my real name instead.  Thanks for asking.<P>Eanre (ToyMaker)||||reg||6
Z||000014||Oreif||03-27-2000||12:42 AM||||I just went to their site and typed in every GM part number for the SD4 and the Fiero race car. (they allow you to search via Part Number) Every Part number came back as Discontinued except one. The Fiero windshield with the Pontiac across the top (it was in between the 2 layers of glass)They call it a racing Windshield. It does not even say it's for a Fiero! It said it could be special ordered in lots of 100.<BR>So if you wanted the windshield for $455.95 we would need 99 other people to buy them first! I wonder if this is covered under my car insurance for glass breakage? Would they pay $45,595.00 Just to replace my windshield? (If I had one like the above) ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Earne||03-27-2000||07:46 AM||||Oreif,<P>No Fiero, but the Pontiac Chieftain race team can still get parts there (grin).  Seems like a plot.  A friend of mine (old HS buddy) is the financial director for GM. He doesn't know a damn thing about the Fiero, but just maybe through him, one day I'll find someone to tell me the truth about this Fiero story (coverup).  <P>Thanks for testing that site, too bad someone at the other end didn't have to manually respond to your requests.  Wonder if they review the query data?<P>Earne (ToyMaker)||||reg||1
Z||000016||Oreif||03-27-2000||11:15 AM||||Here is the official response I got when I inquired about Fiero Parts.<BR>What the *%@#$% Is "not currently available under license!?! Did Pontiac sell the licensing for Fiero's? <P>"Parts for Fiero are not currently available under License.  Suggest you check <BR>with your Pontiac dealer and ask the part manager to check inventory in the <BR>Lansing, Michigan distribution center as discontinued parts are warehoused <BR>and available for sale there until final disposition."<P>GM Order Processing Group<BR>webamster@opgllc.com <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000017||bHooper||03-27-2000||05:34 PM||||today, I called our locall Pontiac Dealership's parts department... my first contact with them in 6 or 7 years... <B>Surpriseingly</B> they were very helpfull!!  I was asking about the plastic speedo gear, they seemed interested and willing to offer information!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>They even made a comment about "how popular those cars are becoming again"... <B>WoW!!</B>  Am I in a time tunnel?  Did I really call the dealership, or did I call Focoa, Ed Parks, or Rodney  with questions??<P>Go figure!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||bHooper||03-28-2000||02:17 PM||||<B>I sent them the following email:</B><P>I have a 1986.5 PONTIAC Fiero GT, and would be interested in being able<BR>to obtain parts from pontiac, in order to properly maintain my car.  As<BR>I plan on keeping this car another 11 years, I would like to have a<BR>quality parts source. I know I am not alone!<P><B>and receieved the following comment in return:</B>  Parts for Fiero are not currently available under license to Restoration <BR>Parts.  Suggest you contact your Pontiac dealer and ask them to check <BR>inventory at the Lansing, Michigan warehouse as discontinued parts are stored <BR>there prior to final disposition.<P>If GM has disposed of the parts, the NOS (New Obsolete Stock) may have been <BR>purchased by Vintage Parts Incorporated who can be reached by email as <BR>follows: sales_dept@dpni.com<P>GM Order Processing Group<BR>webmaster@opgllc.com   <P><B>I emailed Vintage Parts Incorporated, asking for their comment... I am awaiting a answer!</B><BR>||||reg||2
Z||000019||bHooper||03-28-2000||05:46 PM||||<B>WoW!!! I got a answer!  Take a look!</B><P>From: "Sales Department" &lt;customerservice@finlayindustries.com&gt;<BR> 16:44<BR> Subject: Re: Pontiac Fiero restoration parts<BR> To:  "Brian D Hooper" <P>Dear Mr. Hooper,<P>Thanks for your inquiry for the Pontiac Fiero restoration parts.<P><B>Everything we do here is by part number - if you can give us part numbers<BR>for the parts you are looking for, I can tell you if they are available from<BR>Vintage Parts.</B><P>We look forward to hearing from you.<P>Best Regards,<BR>Lois L. Koch<BR>Customer Service Supvr<BR>----- Original Message -----<BR>From: Brian D Hooper <BR>To: &lt;sales_dept@dpni.com&gt;<BR>Sent: Tuesday, March 28, 2000 12:08 PM<BR>Subject: Pontiac Fiero restoration parts<P><BR> The following was emailed to me by "pontiac restoration services"... can you offer any information as to the planed availability of parts for americas only mid engine sports car?<P>Thanks,<BR>Brian Hooper||||reg||10
